  "data_abstract": "We report $e^{\\pm}$\u2212$\\mu^{\\pm}$ pair yield from charm decay measured between midrapidity electrons ($|\\eta|$ < 0.35 and $p_T$ > 0.5 GeV/$c$) and forward rapidity muons (1.4 < $\\eta$ < 2.1 and $p_T$ > 1.0 GeV/$c$) as a function of $\\Delta\\phi$ in both $p$+$p$ and in $d$+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV. Comparing the $p$+$p$ results with several different models, we find the results are consistent with a total charm cross section $\\sigma_{c\\bar{c}}$ = 538 $\\pm$ 46 (stat) $\\pm$ 197 (data syst) $\\pm$ 174 (model syst) $\\mu$b. These generators also indicate that the back-to-back peak at $\\Delta\\phi$ = $\\pi$ is dominantly from the leading order contributions (gluon fusion), while higher order processes (flavor excitation and gluon splitting) contribute to the yield at all $\\Delta\\phi$. We observe a suppression in the pair yield per collision in $d$+Au. We find the pair yield suppression factor for 2.7 < $\\Delta\\phi$ < 3.2 rad is $J_{dA}$ = 0.433 $\\pm$ 0.087 (stat) $\\pm$ 0.135 (syst), indicating cold nuclear matter modification of $c\\bar{c}$ pairs.\n",
